# Routes for https.sh: one line per host name and path of this server.
#   HOST    the full host name browsers use; it goes into the certificate request
#           (the first host is its CN)
#   PATH    starts and ends with /; a / alone takes the whole host
#   PORT    the port the service listens on at 127.0.0.1, or - while it is not known:
#           such a host is in the certificate, and answers 404 until its port is set
#   OPTION  optional: strip, http, api, or several of them separated by commas
#           without spaces, in any order, such as strip,http,api
#           strip: remove PATH before forwarding, for a service that expects /
#           (an API published under /dev/api/). Without it the path is forwarded as is.
#           http: also serve the route on port 80 over plain HTTP, without the redirect
#           to HTTPS, for a TLS front (a WAF or F5) that takes the browsers' HTTPS and
#           connects to this server on port 80. Port 80 then serves the route
#           unencrypted to anybody who can reach it: limit port 80 with a firewall.
#           api: for an API, such as the ISS-Oracle API: PATH docs, PATH redoc and
#           PATH openapi.json (its documentation) answer 404, and each caller
#           address can send at most 10 requests a second, with bursts of 20
#           (429 above that), to all api routes together. Behind a front, the
#           caller address is the front's.
# Other paths of a host answer 404 (on port 80 of a host without http routes: a
# redirect to HTTPS). Everything after # is a comment.
#
# The grey environment: the CN and five SANs of the certificate order (PO
# PM-2026/04/1470), in its order. /dev on the App deployment at port 8110
# (HTTP_PORT in /opt/perodua-app/app.env); WOM and TMS are not served here yet.
# HOST                          PATH        PORT   OPTION
stgiss.perodua.com.my           /dev/       8110
stgissrp.perodua.com.my         /dev/       8110
stgisswom.perodua.com.my        /dev/       -
stgisssp.perodua.com.my         /dev/       8110
stgisscp.perodua.com.my         /dev/       8110
stgisstms.perodua.com.my        /dev/       -
# A UAT deployment at port 8111 later: one /uat/ line per host name.
# stgissrp.perodua.com.my       /uat/       8111
# api.example.perodua.com.my    /dev/api/   8000   strip,api
# Behind a TLS front that connects to port 80, such as a WAF: add http to the line.
# stgiss.perodua.com.my         /dev/       8110   http
